SHA-256 (sha256.c, sha256.h)
===========================

Author:    Brad Conte (brad AT bradconte.com)
Source:    https://github.com/B-Con/crypto-algorithms (sha256.c, sha256.h)
License:   Public domain. The upstream repository states that the code in
           it is released into the public domain; the file headers say it
           is presented "as is" without any guarantees.

The files in this directory are the upstream sources, unchanged. They are
vendored because the catalog needs the SHA-256 of a file's content
(spec 8.5) and the project takes no dependency on a TLS library for it.

The implementation is the FIPS 180-4 SHA-256, little endian byte order.
tests/test_sha256.c checks it against the published test vectors.
